## How Data Flows Through All Four APIs Simultaneously
When a user clicks "Buy Now" on a skin or product, here is the chain reaction utilizing every API:

[ User Browser ]
       │
       ▼ (1) GraphQL Query (Fetches custom dashboard layout)
[ Front-End Gateway ]
       │
       ├──► (2) gRPC Stream (Internal servers talk to Wallet & Inventory instantly)
       │
       └──► (3) SOAP XML Packet (Triggers legacy banking network for escrow transfer)
       │
       ▲ (4) REST API Endpoint (Triggers a webhook notification to an external bot)
[ Partner Script ]

## Why This Matters for Security Testers
When you are assessing a large target platform, you should never assume the whole site behaves the same way. [5] 

* The public paths might be well-secured REST or GraphQL endpoints.
* However, if you look closely at specialized features like file exporting, corporate business-to-business (B2B) portals, or legacy checkout paths, you might discover hidden paths routing to older SOAP architectures or internal configurations that lack the same modern defensive layers. [6] 

